✅ DevOps Networking Learning Roadmap (7 Days Plan)

************************************************************

---

Day 1 – Networking Basics (Very Important)
-------------------------------------------

What is a network?

IP address, Private vs Public IP

Subnetting basic idea

CIDR Notation (e.g. /24)

OSI Model (just overview: 7 layers)

What is DNS, DHCP?


🔁 Practice: Check your IP with ipconfig (Windows) or ip a (Linux)


---

Day 2 – Key Terms for DevOps
------------------------------

What is NAT, SNAT, DNAT?

What is Gateway?

What is Load Balancer?

What is Firewall?

Ports and Protocols (TCP/UDP, 80, 443, 22, etc.)

Ingress vs Egress traffic


🔁 Practice: Use netstat -an and ss -tuln on Linux


---

Day 3 – Networking in Cloud (Azure Focused)
-------------------------------------------

Azure VNet, Subnets

NSG (Network Security Group)

Public IP, Private IP

Azure DNS and Custom DNS

Azure Load Balancer and Application Gateway

VNet Peering

Hub and Spoke model


🔁 Practice: Make a VNet with 2 subnets and ping between VMs


---

Day 4 – Linux Networking Commands (Practical)
----------------------------------------------

ip, ifconfig, ping, traceroute

curl, wget

netstat, ss, nmap

iptables (basic idea)

dig, nslookup


🔁 Practice: Ping external IPs, use curl to test HTTP


---

Day 5 – Docker & Networking
----------------------------

Docker bridge network

Host network, None network

Docker port mapping (-p 8080:80)

Docker DNS

Communication between containers


🔁 Practice: Run 2 containers and connect them via bridge network


---

Day 6 – Terraform, Kubernetes & Networking
-------------------------------------------

Create Azure Networking with Terraform

Define VNet, Subnet, NSG using Terraform

Kubernetes networking overview (Pod IP, Service IP, NodePort, ClusterIP)

Ingress Controller in K8s

Network Policies


🔁 Practice: Create VNet + NSG in Terraform (I'll give you the code if needed)


---

Day 7 – Real-World Scenarios + Interview Questions
--------------------------------------------------

Difference between NSG & Firewall

Why Load Balancer is needed?

How to restrict VM to allow traffic only on port 22?

How traffic flows in Hub & Spoke model?

Common Interview Qs like:

What is VNet Peering?

What is the default port for SSH, HTTPS, etc.?



🔁 Practice: Solve 5-10 networking questions in your notes


